<title>USA: Calif. Diablo Canyon 1,087 MW nuclear to shut Sat.</title>
<headline>Calif. Diablo Canyon 1,087 MW nuclear to shut Sat.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1,087 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Diablo Canyon nuclear power plant in central California will shut early Saturday for a scheduled refueling outage, Pacific Gas &amp; Electric Co confirmed Thursday.</p>
<p>The unit is expected to be out of service for 36 days, a PG&amp;E spokesman said.</p>
<p>Diablo Canyon's 1,073 MW unit 2 was out of service or curtailed between late March and the first half of this month for unplanned repair work.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
